<title>FRANCE: Danone invests in Moroccan dairy sector.</title>
<headline>Danone invests in Moroccan dairy sector.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Groupe Danone said on Tuesday it acquired a 20 percent stake in Centrale Laitiere, a Moroccan company that already produces and markets dairy products under the Danone brandname.</p>
<p>Centrale Laitiere, which is listed on the Casablanca stock market, has annual sales of 1.3 billion francs and a share of some 80 percent of the Moroccan dairy products market, the statement said.</p>
<p>Centrale Laitiere is controlled by private Moroccan group ONA. Since 1974 Danone has owned a 2.74 percent interest in ONA.</p>
<p>ONA and Danone are also planing to strengthen their technical and marketing cooperation.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
